    "created_at": "2024-01-23T17:59:35Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-01-23T17:59:35Z",
    "body": "If it is a copy or a pointer should be unobservable, as long as the \"snapshot state\" behavior is such that if the file changes the File object becomes unreadable (which I think is the only reasonable behavior).\r\n\r\nBut yes, the File API spec is missing the necessary hooks to properly specify this snapshotting behavior (which doesn't just effect this spec, but also things like IndexedDB). It is still somewhere down on my todo list to try to fix that...",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
